csv-lingua
==========

Model weights (model_csv/)
--------------------------
The CSV files in model_csv/ (weights, vocabulary, configuration) are a converted
form of Microsoft's model

    microsoft/llmlingua-2-bert-base-multilingual-cased-meetingbank
    https://huggingface.co/microsoft/llmlingua-2-bert-base-multilingual-cased-meetingbank
    revision 5f0c82792b7ea14c6484e015b6a072009496b7f2

which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The full license text
is in LICENSE-MODEL.txt.

Changes made: the float32 tensors of model.safetensors were written as decimal
text with 7 decimal places (model_csv/, built by convert.py, not in the
repository) and then quantized to 8 bits (model_csv_int8/, the shipped model):
every weight matrix row is stored as one scale plus integers in [-127, 127].
Biases, LayerNorm parameters and the classifier stay as 7-decimal numbers.
The tokenizer vocabulary (vocab.txt) and the 100 tokens [NEW0]..[NEW99] that
llmlingua adds at runtime were written to vocab.csv; config.json and tokenizer
settings were written to config.csv. No weights were retrained or trimmed.

The model is based on BERT-base multilingual cased by Google
(https://github.com/google-research/bert, Apache License 2.0).

Algorithm
---------
The compression steps reimplement Microsoft's LLMLingua-2 as found in
https://github.com/microsoft/LLMLingua (MIT License), commit
5a4c78ae18ab17a98cf997e8259354e546081d64, files llmlingua/prompt_compressor.py
and llmlingua/utils.py.

    Zhuoshi Pan, Qianhui Wu, Huiqiang Jiang, Menglin Xia, Xufang Luo, Jue Zhang,
    Qingwei Lin, Victor Ruhle, Yuqing Yang, Chin-Yew Lin, H. Vicky Zhao, Lili Qiu,
    Dongmei Zhang. "LLMLingua-2: Data Distillation for Efficient and Faithful
    Task-Agnostic Prompt Compression." Findings of ACL 2024. arXiv:2403.12968.

The tokenizer reimplements the behaviour of Hugging Face tokenizers
(https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers, Apache License 2.0).

